# Git and Quality Gates

- Never run destructive git commands unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never force push to protected branches.
- Do not amend commits unless explicitly requested and safe.
- Do not commit automatically; only commit on explicit user request.

## Required Validation Before Hand-off

- Run `yarn check-types` whenever code changes affect TypeScript.
- Run `yarn lint` whenever code style or static checks may be impacted.
- Run `yarn test:ci` for feature-level or regression-sensitive changes.

## Reporting

- Report which checks were executed and whether they passed/failed.
- If checks are skipped, explain why and provide exact follow-up commands.
